Apple's names in NextcloudMailExtension

NextcloudMailExtension is an extension for Mail, the email app in Apple's macOS,
built with Apple's MailKit framework. This repository contains no code, artwork,
icons or other files of Apple's, so this repository's MIT licence (LICENSE)
covers only the project's own work. The symbols the app shows, such as the eye
beside the password field, are SF Symbols, which macOS draws while the app runs.
The website's screenshots show Apple's interface, as described below.

Apple, AppleScript, Finder, iCloud, Keychain, Mac, macOS, Mail Drop, Safari,
SF Symbols, Spotlight, Swift, SwiftUI and Xcode are trademarks of Apple Inc.,
registered in the U.S. and other countries and regions.

NextcloudMailExtension is not made, endorsed or supported by Apple Inc.


Mail and the tools

- Mail is part of macOS and comes under the macOS licence. This project doesn't
  include or change it. Its About window says: "Mail, Version 16.0
  (3901.100.1.1.12), © 1995–2025 Apple Inc. All rights reserved."
- The project builds with Xcode and Apple's SDKs, which come under Apple's own
  licence agreements.


The website's screenshots

The project's website, in site/, shows how the extension works with Mail. Its
screenshots, in site/media/screenshots/, are the project's own, taken on macOS,
and show Apple's interface as macOS draws it:

- mail-send-overview-annotated.png and mail-send-popup.png: Mail's message
  window, its toolbar and its symbols.
- mail-send-large-annotated.png: Mail's prompt that offers Mail Drop, with its
  iCloud symbol.
- mail-receive-overview.png: Mail's window showing a received message.
- mail-settings-ext-merged.png: Mail's Settings window, on its Extensions tab.
- server-dir.png: Safari's window and toolbar.
- app-overview.png: the project's own app, in a macOS window.

Apple's interface in them, its windows, controls, symbols and icons, is Apple's
and isn't covered by this repository's MIT licence. The annotations, the example
email and the project's app and extension are the project's own.


Sources

- Guidelines for Using Apple Trademarks and Copyrights:
  https://www.apple.com/legal/intellectual-property/guidelinesfor3rdparties.html
- Apple's trademark list:
  https://www.apple.com/legal/intellectual-property/trademark/appletmlist.html


Terms

Apple's guidelines allow naming Apple's products to say what a product works
with, in phrases such as "for use with" or "compatible with", as long as Apple's
name isn't part of the product's name. They also say: "You may not use or
register, in whole or in part, Apple, ... or any other Apple trademark" as, or as
part of, a company, product or service name. The project's name,
NextcloudMailExtension, contains no Apple trademark, and the project names Apple's
products only to say what it works with.
